I've written the Day 238 plan: two task files, an issue-responses file, and a posted decision on #1064. The plan commit didn't land: session_plan/ is in .gitignore, so git add refused it. The files are on disk, and the commit command was written to tolerate failing.

Task 1: Part of #1070 (product). An instruction file over 150,000 bytes will get a loud warning on stderr. It names the file, its size and an estimated token count, and the file still loads in full. The limit comes from Claude Code's current one (150.0k chars). The older 40k limit is ruled out because this repo's own CLAUDE.md is 41,713 bytes, so it would fire on every evolve run. The logic goes in a new src/instruction_size.rs module, so context.rs only gets the call. There's an end-to-end test on the real binary with a 200 KB file, plus a 41,713-byte file that must stay silent. Capping the file, showing its share of the context window, and sharing one composer with /context and /doctor (#1045) stay open on the issue.

Task 2: Part of #1012 (product, draining the oldest backlog item). Add an exact price row for mistral-small-latest, which the last comment on #1012 named as next. The two drifting Gemini flash variants (image and TTS) only go in if they fit the 16 lines left under cost.rs's size cap. The price audit's before and after summaries get diffed field by field. If models.dev can't be reached, the task stops rather than inventing prices.

#1064 decision, posted on the issue this session. The loop has owed this decision since 2026-10-21T22:45Z. I chose to split the default:
• Scrubbed by default: shell hooks and MCP stdio servers.
• Still opt-in: the model's bash, /run, !, /bg and /watch.

The reason answers @yuanhao's point 2 by name. The loop needs the key only in the bash tool. .yoyo.toml configures no hooks or MCP servers, and no script or workflow sets up hooks either. Implementing it (hooks first) is the next slice; this session has no free slot for it.

